@nsobid-6C4BC35D955FABDEF98616FA93F38FAF49B5FE48

# Clubhouse Games 51 Worldwide Classics 2.0.1 - 2560x1440 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Renders at 2560x1440 in both docked and handheld mode.
//
// The engine keeps three sizes: a window size that every display texture is
// allocated at and that caps everything else, a per-mode render size for the
// 3D scene (stage 0) and the final image (stage 1), and a base resolution
// (1920x1080) that viewports and layouts are authored in. Stock docked play
// renders stage 0 at 1600x900 or 1920x1080 and stage 1 at 1920x1080, and
// every render size is clamped to the window size.
//
// The engine ships a developer high-resolution mode behind one flag in
// bex::SystemMain (+0x294). When set, boot applies 3840x2160 to both modes,
// the nd::NdRender render-target slot table is allocated at twice its
// 1920x1080 dimensions, and SetRenderingResolutionModeNormal/Boost and
// ResetParameter stop lowering the render size per scene. Every read of that
// flag is forced to 1 here, the fixed boot size is changed from 3840x2160
// to 2560x1440, and the window size is pinned so the clamp lets the full
// size through. The base resolution is left alone, so viewports, UI and
// cameras keep their 1920x1080 coordinate space.
//
// Two GPU memory pools scale with the render size and are enlarged: pool 3
// (display and renderer targets, 128 MB) and pool 4 (engine render textures
// and the cascaded shadow map, 128 MB). Pool 4 also leaves room for the
// [Shadow Resolution 4096] mod. The pool sizes are the engine's built-in
// defaults; boot.lua can in principle override them.
//
// REQUIRES Ryujinx > System > DRAM Size set to 6 GiB or higher. All of the
// above comes out of the main heap. At boot the game reserves every byte of
// application memory as one block, but then hands its allocator at most
// 0xC7500000 (about 3.19 GB) of it, so any larger DRAM setting is wasted
// and asset loading fails once the bigger buffers are in. The allocator is
// given the whole reserved block instead.
//
// This mod OWNS the pool and heap offsets below; do not duplicate them in
// another enabled mod.

@enabled
// Main heap: pass the full reserved block to the allocator.
007C8BC4 F40315AA   // MOV X20,X21 = full heap size (was CSEL X20,X9,X21,HI = 3.19 GB cap)
// High-resolution mode flag readers (were LDR W8,[Xn,#0x294]).
0022C65C 28008052   // MOVZ W8,#1  boot: apply the fixed render size to both modes
0022F5B4 28008052   // MOVZ W8,#1  nd::NdRender: double the render-target slot pool
00230CEC 28008052   // MOVZ W8,#1  ResetParameter: skip per-scene render sizes
00231468 28008052   // MOVZ W8,#1  SetRenderingResolutionModeNormal: ignore
002314CC 28008052   // MOVZ W8,#1  SetRenderingResolutionModeBoost: ignore
// Fixed boot render size.
0022C66C 16B48052   // MOVZ W22,#1440 (was 2160)
0022C674 02408152   // MOVZ W2,#2560  (was 3840, docked)
0022C68C 02408152   // MOVZ W2,#2560  (was 3840, handheld)
// Window size, the clamp for every render size (stock 1920x1080).
00689064 09408152   // MOVZ W9,#2560 (was LDR W9,[X1,#0x64])
00689078 09B48052   // MOVZ W9,#1440 (was LDR W9,[X1,#0x68])
// GPU memory pool defaults in .rodata (group 0, both were 0x08000000 = 128 MB).
00FC3FF8 00000010   // pool 3 = 256 MB
00FC3FFC 00000018   // pool 4 = 384 MB
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Clubhouse Games 51 Worldwide Classics
// 2.0.1 (NdCube Bezel engine + nd::NdRender, NVN). The retail build keeps only
// a partial symbol table; every site was located by structure and
// byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
